-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 68 DOWN: no-op.
--
-- Migration 68 defines the `related_note` edge table as
-- ``TYPE RELATION FROM note TO note`` (the shape the Track Y auto-link feature
-- needs) and adds its fields (`similarity_score`, `method`, `created_at`). It is
-- a forward-only schema definition with no faithful inverse (mirrors migrations
-- 66/67's down):
--   * reverting `related_note` to TYPE ANY would re-break
--     ``RELATE note -> related_note -> note`` — exactly the correctness 68
--     establishes; and
--   * `related_note` is a DERIVED, regenerated projection (auto-link clears and
--     re-relates a note's links) — the edge table holds no canonical state worth
--     a destructive rollback, and on this corpus it is empty until auto-link runs.
-- Down intentionally does nothing; mirrors migrations 66/67's down convention.
-- ============================================================================
